    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(x\\lt0,\\) each of \\(x^6,-3x^5,-6x^3,-x,\\) and \\(8\\) is positive, so there is no negative root. At \\(x=0\\) the polynomial is \\(8,\\) while at \\(x=1\\) it is \\(-1.\\) Continuity therefore gives a positive root between \\(0\\) and \\(1.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Determine the sign of every term when \\(x\\lt0\\)",
        "Compare the polynomial’s values at \\(0\\) and \\(1\\)"
      ],
